' 57 The VerificationBytes of one receive against the records of its
' collection, for each discipline, with the host-work limit of protocol
' version 6. Decision 89 retired that limit. The chart keeps the measurement
' before decision 89, and the next timed run replaces it.
'
' Source of Figure 2 of ../performance.md (section 3.3). The measured points
' are the receive_from_n cases of test-vectors/reified-bench-contract-v1.json
' that fit the limit. Each line is the least-squares line of Table 5 of that
' document, drawn from 0 records to the size where it reaches the limit:
'     bag: 1,267 records
'     set: 907 records
'     queue and stack: 1,136 records
'     priority queue: 993 records
'     VectorDB: 433 records
' The queue and the stack have one line, because their lines differ by less
' than 0.1 %. The host program reserved 0.36 million at every size, so
' the chart does not draw it apart from the axis. The numbers come from the
' contract, so a new contract needs a new source and a new rendering.
'
' Colors come from the shared palette.
' Render: ./render.sh 57-receive-host-work.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startchart 57-receive-host-work
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
title The VerificationBytes of one receive against the records of its collection (before decision 89)
h-axis "records of the collection" 0 --> 1400 spacing 200
v-axis "millions of VerificationBytes" 0 --> 300 spacing 50 grid
line "v6 limit (retired)" [(0, 268.44), (1400, 268.44)] $ca_neutral
line "bag" [(0, 3.06), (1267, 268.44)] $ca_instantiate
line "set" [(0, 3.13), (907, 268.44)] $ca_debit
line "queue and stack" [(0, 5.18), (1136, 268.44)] $ca_credit
line "priority queue" [(0, 5.21), (993, 268.44)] $ca_rejectfill
line "VectorDB" [(0, 5.94), (433, 268.44)] $ca_gate
scatter <<circle>> "measured" [(10, 5.29), (100, 23.87), (1000, 212.54), (10, 6.05), (100, 32.39), (10, 7.50), (100, 28.34), (1000, 236.82), (10, 7.50), (100, 28.35), (1000, 236.82), (10, 7.86), (100, 31.72), (10, 12.00), (100, 66.55)] $ca_neutral
legend right
@endchart
